<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d11" for="edge" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d10" for="edge" attr.name="seq" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d9" for="edge" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d8" for="edge" attr.name="flow_id" attr.type="long" />
  <key id="d7" for="node" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d6" for="node" attr.name="service" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="node" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="graph" attr.name="graph_usable" attr.type="boolean" />
  <key id="d3" for="graph" attr.name="categories" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d2" for="graph" attr.name="notes" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="graph" attr.name="link" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="graph" attr.name="name" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="directed">
    <node id="0">
      <data key="d5">Dev</data>
      <data key="d6">UserCompanyDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d7">Developer commits code changes, build definitions and CloudFormation templates to the repository; can modify build and infrastructure on demand by going back to the first stage.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="1">
      <data key="d5">CODECOMMIT</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeCommit</data>
      <data key="d7">AWS source repository (first pipeline stage). Holds application code, build configuration and the CloudFormation templates that define the entire application infrastructure.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2">
      <data key="d5">CODEBUILD</data>
      <data key="d6">CodeBuild</data>
      <data key="d7">Build stage. Spins up a container and is paid only for the build duration; build behaviour is controlled by the developer through the repository. On a successful build it outputs a container image to ECR.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3">
      <data key="d5">REGISTRY</data>
      <data key="d6">ECR</data>
      <data key="d7">Amazon ECR registry holding the application container image, ready to be deployed.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="4">
      <data key="d5">CLOUDFORMATION</data>
      <data key="d6">CloudFormation</data>
      <data key="d7">Third (deploy) stage, chosen over CodeDeploy, the ECS task definition deployer and Lambda because the infrastructure is deployed along with the app. A single baseline template is used for all production environments; parallel stages cover up to 100 customers/VPCs, each with a small configuration (VPC name, ECS cluster). Three-step governance: 1) ChangeSet, 2) Approve/reject by someone with the proper roles, 3) Execute.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="5">
      <data key="d5">VPC</data>
      <data key="d6">VPC</data>
      <data key="d7">Target production VPC; each customer is deployed to a different VPC (up to 100). Contains ECS, IAM and ALB.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="6">
      <data key="d5">ECS</data>
      <data key="d6">ECS</data>
      <data key="d7">Elastic Container Service task definition running the application image; deployed by CloudFormation.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="7">
      <data key="d5">IAM</data>
      <data key="d6">IAM</data>
      <data key="d7">IAM roles and permissions required by the application; deployed by CloudFormation.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="8">
      <data key="d5">ALB</data>
      <data key="d6">ALB</data>
      <data key="d7">Application Load Balancer required by the application; deployed by CloudFormation.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="9">
      <data key="d5">CODEPIPELINE</data>
      <data key="d6">CodePipeline</data>
      <data key="d7">Pipeline orchestrating the stages (source -&gt; build -&gt; deploy), moving each commit to the next stage. Drawn on the board without explicit arrows.</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="0" target="1" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Developer commits code changes to the CodeCommit repository.</data>
      <data key="d10">0</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1" target="2" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">The pipeline moves the commit to the next stage, CodeBuild.</data>
      <data key="d10">1</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="3" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">After a successful build, CodeBuild outputs the application container image to the ECR registry.</data>
      <data key="d10">2</data>
      <data key="d11">data</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2" target="4" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">Once the build is done and the image is in the registry, the CloudFormation deploy stage is kicked off (ChangeSet -&gt; Approve -&gt; Execute).</data>
      <data key="d10">3</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="5" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation executes the approved change set and deploys to the VPC; in parallel to up to 100 customer VPCs.</data>
      <data key="d10">4</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="6" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the ECS task definition with the application image.</data>
      <data key="d10">4'</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="7" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the IAM role and permissions.</data>
      <data key="d10">4''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4" target="8" id="0">
      <data key="d8">0</data>
      <data key="d9">CloudFormation deploys the Application Load Balancer.</data>
      <data key="d10">4'''</data>
      <data key="d11">control</data>
    </edge>
    <data key="d0">Aetion: Streamlined CI/CD for Application and Infrastructure with CodePipeline and CloudFormation</data>
    <data key="d1">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6YkguepAQuQ</data>
    <data key="d2">Healthcare analytics company pipeline that takes a developer commit through CodeCommit, CodeBuild, and ECR, then a CloudFormation deploy stage (ChangeSet, Approve, Execute) that deploys ECS task definitions, IAM roles and ALBs into per-customer VPCs, with parallel stages for up to 100 customers.</data>
    <data key="d3">DevOps, CI/CD, Containers, Infrastructure as Code</data>
    <data key="d4">True</data>
  </graph>
</graphml>
